1
00:03:54,545 --> 00:04:00,545
The Muppet Christmas Carol is a music, comedy,
family film directed by Brian Henson.

2
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:55,090
A retelling of the classic Dickens tale of
Ebenezer Scrooge, miser extraordinaire.

3
00:11:43,636 --> 00:11:49,636
He is held accountable for his dastardly ways during night-time
visitations by the Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present and Future.

4
00:15:38,181 --> 00:15:44,181
Ebenezer Scrooge, played by Michael Caine.

5
00:19:32,727 --> 00:19:38,727
The Great Gonzo as Charles Dickens / Robert Marley / Dr. Bunsen Honeydew /
Betina Cratchit / Rat / Zoot (voice), played by Dave Goelz.

6
00:23:27,272 --> 00:23:33,272
Kermit the Frog as Bob Cratchit / Rizzo the Rat / Beaker / Bean Bunny / Belinda
Cratchit / Beetle / Lips / Pig Gentleman (voice), played by Steve Whitmire.

7
00:27:21,818 --> 00:27:27,818
Tiny Tim Cratchit / Jacob Marley / Ghost of Christmas Present / Lew Zealand / Ma Bear / Mouse / Mr.
Applegate / Penguin / Pig Gentleman / Pops / Rat (voice), played by Jerry Nelson.

8
00:31:16,363 --> 00:31:22,363
Miss Piggy as Emily Cratchit / Fozzie Bear as Fozziewig / Sam the Eagle as Headmaster of Junior High Graduates /
Animal / George the Janitor / Horse and Carriage Driver / Vegetable Salesman (voice), played by Frank Oz.

9
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:16,909
Rat / Peter Cratchit / Old Joe / Swedish Chef (voice), played by David Rudman.

10
00:39:05,454 --> 00:39:11,454
The Muppet Christmas Carol is a 1992 American Christmas musical film produced
and directed by Brian Henson (in his feature directorial debut).

11
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
It is the fourth theatrical film featuring the Muppets.

12
00:46:54,545 --> 00:47:00,545
Adapted from the 1843 novella A Christmas Carol by Charles Dickens with a screenplay written by Jerry Juhl, the film
takes artistic license to suit the aesthetic of the Muppets, but follows Dickens' original story closely.

13
00:50:49,090 --> 00:50:55,090
It is the first Muppet film where a human is the main protagonist.

14
00:54:43,636 --> 00:54:49,636
The film stars Michael Caine as Ebenezer Scrooge alongside Muppet
performers Dave Goelz, Steve Whitmire, Jerry Nelson, and Frank Oz.

15
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:44,181
It is the first Muppet film to be produced following the deaths of creator Jim
Henson and performer Richard Hunt; the film is dedicated to both.

16
01:02:32,727 --> 01:02:38,727
The film was released in the United States on December 11, 1992, by Buena
Vista Pictures Distribution under its Walt Disney Pictures label.

17
01:06:27,272 --> 01:06:33,272
It was a modest box office success and received generally favorable reviews.

18
01:10:21,818 --> 01:10:27,818
It is the first Muppets film to be produced by Disney, whose parent company would
later acquire the rights to the Muppets characters and assets in 2004.

19
01:14:16,363 --> 01:14:22,363
The film's reputation has grown in the years since its release, and it is
often listed as one of the best Christmas films of all time.

20
01:18:10,909 --> 01:18:16,909
The film explores themes of future, london, england,
based on novel or book, holiday, redemption.

21
01:22:05,454 --> 01:22:11,454
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
